desc:NH4X Volca Drum Panel
// VOLCA DRUM PANEL 2.6.2 by NH4X - editor + display for the Korg volca drum, as one JSFX.
// Part of the NH4X Volca Drum Suite: https://github.com/NH4Xnet/volca-drum-suite  (manual + setup in the README there)
// Music: https://nh4x.bandcamp.com/
//
// SETUP
//  1. Install via ReaPack (repository above), then add "JS: NH4X Volca Drum Panel" to a track.
//     With the NH4X Volca Drum Sequencer: sequencer FIRST, panel after it on the same track.
//  2. Track: MIDI hardware output = the port your volca drum is connected to (send to original channels).
//  3. Volca: split channel mode (part 1-6 = MIDI channel 1-6, see the Korg manual). Waveguide CCs go out on channel 1.
//  4. FILT and CLIP (purple row names) need the custom firmware "vdcf" 1.22 by hj-oja (CC 54/55);
//     on the stock Korg firmware they do nothing. Everything else works on stock firmware.
//  5. Run the action "Volca listener (start)" once and answer Yes (sound SAVE / RENAME / DELETE need it).
//
// USE
//  - Drag or mouse wheel = change, double-click or Alt+click = default, hover + type 0-127 + Enter = exact value.
//    Rest the mouse 1 s on a button = what it does (in the display).
//  - SELECT is shown as three rows: SRC (source), MOD.T (modulation type), EG.T (envelope type).
//    Each row changes only its own part. Still one Select CC underneath (n = value x 45 / 128).
//  - The volca has no MIDI out: the panel only knows what it sent. SEND ALL pushes the whole kit.
//    AUTO SEND (on by default) sends the whole kit once after a project load.
//  - Kits = REAPER presets of this plugin (preset menu at the top of the FX window). Loading one sends the changes.
//    Actions "Volca kit (save)" / "(kit +)" / "(kit -)" / "(send all)" do the same from a key or controller.
//  - Click a part title = select that part. LINK = changes on one layer go to the other layer too.
//    Play button = one test hit on that part. Q = pitch quantize (QPI, CC 53) for that part.
//  - SOUND (or right-click a part title): copy / paste a part, LOAD a sound file; SAVE / RENAME / DELETE need the listener.
//    Sound files: REAPER resource folder / Data / NH4X Volca / VolcaSounds (shared by all projects).
//  - RANDOM: target (part / L1 / L2 / kit), kind, amount, ROLL, UNDO (also undoes a paste; press again = redo).
//    SMART rolls a sound of the chosen kind (KICK ... MICRO, MIX = a drum kit on KIT) inside its useful ranges,
//    WILD rolls anything, full range. Low amount = stay close to the current sound.
//    Locks (amber) are skipped by every roll: right-click (or Shift+click) a bar = one cell,
//    click a row name = that row in this part, right-click a row name = that row in all parts,
//    Shift+click a part title = whole part. Locks are saved with the project, not in presets.
//  - MORPH: SET A, SET B (snapshots of the whole kit, saved with the project), then move the bar.
//    Select and WG Model switch at 50 %. Locked cells don't move.
//  - LOOK (small square, top left) = Sleeve (default) / Classic. COLOR (swatch next to it) = 14 color themes (click or wheel).
//    Sleeve: big numbers + titles in the free font "Big Shoulders Display" if installed (Google Fonts), otherwise
//    Bahnschrift Condensed; all other text in Bahnschrift SemiBold SemiCondensed (comes with Windows 10/11).
//  - Note routing: notes 65/67/69/71/72/74 on any channel go out on channel 1-6 (= part 1-6),
//    so one piano roll on one channel plays all parts. Notes on channel 11-16 go to part 1-6 unchanged
//    (play a part melodically, best with Q on). All other MIDI passes through.
//  - All parameters are plugin parameters: automation and MIDI controllers work.
//    Sliders 146 Roll / 147 Undo act as buttons (1 = fire), 148 = Morph.
//    Sliders 160-195 = each Select row (SRC / MOD.T / EG.T) as its own parameter, per part and layer;
//    they follow the panel, and moving one changes only its own part of the Select CC.
//
// CC numbers: Korg "volca drum MIDI Implementation Chart (Split channel)" 2019.2.20 + vdcf README (54 FLT, 55 CLP),
// QPI CC 53 from the Synthmata volca drum editor. Fonts: Bahnschrift + Consolas (Windows).

options:no_meter gmem=NH4XVolca
in_pin:none
out_pin:none

